{
 "_doc": "The watermark pass (Pierre, 2026-11-15, Q373; judging/FISH.md \"Watermark\"): the fish photos Home can show (each family's cover and the reference photos its band rotates through, up to 10 per family in the game's order) judged by eye on their R2 file; each one listed carries a visible watermark or text (a photographer's name, a logo, a copyright line), with what the judge saw. python3 tools/judging_fish.py watermark writes the flag w into its single judgement; Home skips it, the games keep it; Pierre takes the flag off in the admin like any tag. The second pass (ROADMAP \"Watermark pass, the rest\") looked at 1,153 band-kind photos the first did not reach, so looked adds the two passes' counts (844 + 1,153); a few photos past the first pass's 10 per family may have been looked at in both, so it is not a count of distinct photos. The second pass also looked again at 21 photos of the first pass's count (the band-kind photos in each family's first 10 by the authors it tagged). The third pass (ROADMAP \"Watermark pass, the rest\", Q373) looked at the 897 photos the Identify art and a Home tile can fall back on (home.js tilePhoto) under any re-sort of the ratings that no pass had looked at; looked adds them (2,894 in all). It also looked again at 98 photos Home can show, looked at by an earlier pass, by the authors it tagged (not counted in looked). The reference-photo batch of 2026-11-16 looked at the 28 reference photos it judged, each at 1024 px (the original where smaller), its top and bottom bands enlarged: looked adds them (2,922 in all). The fourth pass (2026-11-19) looked at the 52 photos the refills of 2026-11-16 to 2026-11-18 brought into fish-game.json since then (57 in all, 5 of them already listed by the batch above), each R2 file (-m) on a contact sheet at 560 px with contrast raised, then its top 12% and bottom 25% at 700 px; the corners of the 3 by authors tagged before seen again at 2x: looked adds them (2,974 in all). 1 new tag; 7 of the 52 were found to carry a mark that their judged code already flagged w, and are listed here with what was seen.",
